<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingkitsarath</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1713</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kingkitsarath was the first king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luang-prabang">Luang Prabang</a>, a grandson of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sourigna-vongsa">Sourigna Vongsa</a> of Lan Xang. After succession disputes divided Lan Xang, he established himself at Luang Prabang in 1707 with support from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xishuangbanna">Sipsongpanna</a>, creating a kingdom separate from Vientiane. He ruled there until his death in 1713.</p></div>
